  "node.title": "Node Explorer",
  "node.help.title": "How nodes and edges are built from documents",
  "node.help.content": "<p>When you sync a documentation source, DocGraph automatically builds a knowledge graph:</p><dl><dt><strong>Nodes</strong> — entities extracted from your docs:</dt><dd><strong>Product</strong> — created from the optional \"Product\" field on a source. Groups related docs together.</dd><dd><strong>Module</strong> — created from the optional \"Module\" field. Represents a sub-component of a product.</dd><dd><strong>Document</strong> — one node per document (Markdown file, HTML page, etc.).</dd><dd><strong>DocSection</strong> — one node per heading/section within a document.</dd><dd><strong>API</strong> — extracted from HTTP method + path patterns in the text (e.g. <code>GET /api/users</code>).</dd></dl><dl><dt><strong>Edges</strong> — relationships between nodes:</dt><dd><strong>contains</strong> — nesting (Product→Module, Document→DocSection).</dd><dd><strong>describes</strong> — a product/module describes a document; or a section describes an API (OpenAPI docs).</dd><dd><strong>mentions</strong> — a DocSection mentions an API.</dd><dd><strong>exposes_api</strong> — a document/product/module exposes an API.</dd><dd><strong>links_to</strong> — HTML &lt;a&gt; links between sections.</dd></dl><p>Node IDs are deterministic — resyncing the same source produces the same graph.</p>",
  "node.search": "Search Nodes",
